<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Experiment 1 - GitHub Basics</title>

    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        }

        body {
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
            color: #222;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        header {
            background-color: #24292e;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 40px 20px;
        }

        header h1 {
            font-size: 32px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        header p {
            color: #ccc;
        }

        .container {
            width: 90%;
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 30px auto;
        }

        .card {
            background: white;
            padding: 25px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }

        .card h2 {
            margin-bottom: 15px;
            color: #24292e;
        }

        .card ul {
            margin-left: 25px;
        }

        code {
            background: #eee;
            padding: 4px 7px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            color: #c7254e;
        }

        .steps {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
            gap: 15px;
            margin-top: 15px;
        }

        .step {
            background: #f8f9fa;
            padding: 18px;
            border-left: 4px solid #24292e;
        }

        .step h3 {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            background: #24292e;
            color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            margin-top: 40px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Experiment 1</h1>
        <p>GitHub Repository Setup, Branching, Merging & GitHub Pages</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">

        <div class="card">
            <h2>Aim</h2>
            <p>
                To understand GitHub repository creation, file management,
                branching, merging and hosting a webpage using GitHub Pages.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>Objectives</h2>

            <ul>
                <li>Create and manage a GitHub repository.</li>
                <li>Upload and organize files using folders.</li>
                <li>Create and work with branches.</li>
                <li>Merge changes into the main branch.</li>
                <li>Host a webpage using GitHub Pages.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>GitHub Workflow</h2>

            <div class="steps">

                <div class="step">
                    <h3>1. Repository</h3>
                    <p>Create a repository to store the project files.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="step">
                    <h3>2. Branch</h3>
                    <p>Create a separate branch to work on changes.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="step">
                    <h3>3. Commit</h3>
                    <p>Save changes to the repository using commits.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="step">
                    <h3>4. Merge</h3>
                    <p>Merge the completed branch into the main branch.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="step">
                    <h3>5. GitHub Pages</h3>
                    <p>Publish the HTML webpage online using GitHub Pages.</p>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>Important Git Commands</h2>

            <p><code>git init</code> - Initialize a Git repository.</p>
            <br>

            <p><code>git add .</code> - Add files to staging.</p>
            <br>

            <p><code>git commit -m "message"</code> - Save changes.</p>
            <br>

            <p><code>git branch</code> - View available branches.</p>
            <br>

            <p><code>git merge</code> - Merge branches.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>Result</h2>

            <p>
                A GitHub repository was successfully created and organized.
                The concepts of branching, committing, merging and GitHub Pages
                hosting were studied and implemented.
            </p>
        </div>

    </div>

    <footer>
        <p>Web Development Lab | Experiment 1</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>